    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nThe `ui_busy_start/stop` pair around the \"written\" message (#25974, added in #29447) no longer serves a purpose on current main. Tested all four combos (foot + Neovide, with and without the pair), saving via `:nnoremap <silent> w :write<CR>`:\r\n\r\n- foot: cursor still leaves the editor for the cmdline with the pair in place; removing it changes nothing there.\r\n- Neovide: no flicker and no cursor-animation jump either way; the pair only adds a hide/show flicker.\r\n- Nothing sets busy during the actual file I/O; this is the only `ui_busy_start` in the whole write path, so the pair cannot be signaling busyness. Busy indication for writes is owned by `filemess_progress`.\r\n\r\nEnv: NixOS 26.11pre (kernel 7.2.9, Wayland), foot 1.28.0, Neovide nightly-39+g802c67f, nvim at 326d764e3e.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nDrop the calls, along with the regression test that locked them in (it only asserted the busy events, never actual cursor visibility).\r\n\r\nNote: this PR started as gating the pair on silent writes; per discussion below it now drops the pair entirely.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-18T14:42:43Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
