            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think this is a misdiagnosis. Alternative: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42452\r\n\r\nUI events are batched, so busy_stop reaches the UI at the next flush, which happens after unchanged(), undofile write, and BufWritePost/FileWritePost handlers. \r\n\r\nIf we remove everything as in this PR, GUIs won't get \"busy\" signal during writes (which may include arbitrarily slow `BufWritePost` handlers).\r\n\r\nThe change I suggested (do `ui_busy_start()` before `filemess_progress()`) is meaningful.",
